  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/c4cc5ffd-4e6c-4bd7-967f-6091be0cf637-1b833bce-44a7-4fda-bf61-d9df17d1fa51-image.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 125px;\" /></p><p>Let the charged particle be displaced slightly towards right by distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8810;</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math>, towards right</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>at</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math>, towards left</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mover><mi>F</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover><mi>F</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mover><mi>F</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, will bring it towards <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math>.<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mi>F</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msub><mi>&#1013;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mstyle><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>Q</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msub><mi>&#1013;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow><msup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mfenced><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p>Since <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8810;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is negligible.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mi>F</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><msub><mi>&#1013;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>x</mi><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p>Clearly, the direction of the force is opposite to the displacement &amp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>&#8733;</mo><mi>x</mi></math>, hence it is an SHM.</p><p>Acceleration of charged particle is given as,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>F</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><msub><mi>&#1013;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>And we know that for SHM,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Comparing <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math>, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><msub><mi>&#1013;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p>Hence, the&nbsp;time period,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mi>&#969;</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><msub><mi>&#1013;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p>Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math></p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
